Kitty graphics
==============

This implementation is adapted from Sergei Grechanik's st-graphics patch:
https://st.suckless.org/patches/kitty-graphics-protocol/
st-kitty-graphics-20251230-0.9.3.diff, based on graphics commit eb8d6cb.
The original MIT notices are preserved in the imported source files.

Protocol specification:
https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/graphics-protocol/

Build
-----
Install the development packages for Imlib2 and zlib in addition to the
existing X11, Xft, Xrender, Fontconfig, FreeType, and HarfBuzz dependencies.
On Debian, the additional package names are libimlib2-dev and zlib1g-dev.

If you maintain config.h, merge the graphics configuration and anysize
alignment settings from config.def.h before rebuilding. A pre-existing
config.h is never replaced by make. Keep your fonts, colors, and shortcuts.

Build with make, and install the updated terminfo with tic -sx st.info.

Display images
--------------
With Kitty's standalone kitten executable installed:

    kitten icat image.png

For an SSH session, force transfer through the terminal stream:

    kitten icat --transfer-mode=stream image.png

The included helper is installed as st-icat by make install:

    st-icat image.png
    st-icat -m direct image.png

Before installing, it can be run as ./icat-mini.sh. The helper requires
ImageMagick. The terminal itself does not require ImageMagick or kitty.

Keep TERM=st-256color. Clients can probe the graphics protocol; clients which
only recognize terminal brands may need their graphics backend selected
explicitly. Avoid changing TERM globally to impersonate another terminal.

In tmux, enable passthrough:

    set -g allow-passthrough on

The application must send graphics commands through tmux and use Unicode
placeholders to make image cells follow its layout. The tmux terminal entry
must advertise RGB colors. SSH and tmux application combinations are not
covered by the local Xvfb checks.

Supported behavior
------------------
* PNG and raw RGB/RGBA uploads, including zlib-compressed raw data.
* Chunked direct transfers, regular files, temporary files, and POSIX shared
  memory. Local file/shared-memory transfers require a shared filesystem.
* Capability queries, acknowledgements, and error responses.
* Image IDs, placement IDs, cropping, and placement dimensions.
* Classic placements and Unicode placeholders; images follow terminal cells
  through scrollback and screen changes.
* Deleting classic placements restores their saved text where available.
* SGR underline colors/styles, used by Unicode placeholders for placement IDs.
* Pixel-size queries used by image clients.

The integration preserves box drawing, HarfBuzz shaping, transparent
backgrounds, input-method handling, and the existing scrollback behavior.
Image placeholder metadata is excluded from HarfBuzz shaping.

Configuration and shortcuts
---------------------------
config.def.h contains image file/RAM/cache limits and the cache-directory
template. Defaults allow a 20 MiB upload, a 100 MiB decoded image, a 300 MiB
disk cache, and 300 MiB of image RAM. Cache limits use the upstream eviction
policy; they are not strict process-wide memory limits.

Graphics shortcuts use GRAPHICSMOD (Ctrl+Shift), independently of TERMMOD:

    Ctrl+Shift+right click   Open the image in feh, if installed.
    Ctrl+Shift+middle click  Inspect image metadata.
    Ctrl+Shift+F1            Cycle graphics diagnostics.
    Ctrl+Shift+F6            Dump image/cache state to stderr.
    Ctrl+Shift+F7            Unload image data from RAM.
    Ctrl+Shift+F8            Toggle image rendering.

The imported anysize support centers the terminal grid inside the window by
default. Adjust anysize_halign and anysize_valign in config.h if desired.

Limits
------
This is a subset of the Kitty graphics protocol, not a complete equivalent
of the kitty terminal:

* Placements support up to 511 rows/columns and 24-bit placement IDs.
* Z-index, overlapping layers, relative placements, and deletion by pixel or
  cursor position are not supported. Classic placements occupy terminal cells.
* Animation support is inherited and experimental; frame composition/deletion
  and explicit loop counts are not fully implemented.
* Partial-file offsets are not implemented. Shared-memory offsets are supported.
* Inline image decoding depends on the Imlib2 loaders installed on the system.

Validation
----------
    make check

The Python standard-library tests launch st in Xvfb, drive a real child PTY,
and read X11 pixels. They cover raw/PNG/RGBA/compressed uploads, chunking,
local files and shared memory, Unicode placeholders, cursor policy, deletion,
scrollback, alternate screens, SGR subparameters, and invalid transfers.
